---
/**
 * Academy (the academy view of the client's design): the curriculum, why these skills matter, the Academy's
 * collections with their logos (pick one to see what is in it), and how every lesson ends with a rep.
 *
 * The collections were the design's twelve topics with stock photos until November 4, when Leah asked for the
 * Academy's own logos ("Can you swap these out with academy logos :) in our drive"): now each is one of the
 * Academy's collections, its logo, the approved line about it, and its courses where the app has them.
 */
import Layout from "../layouts/Practice.astro";
import { COLLECTIONS } from "../data/practice";

/** What the panel under the grid says for a collection: worked out here, so the page and its script agree. */
const VIEW = COLLECTIONS.map((c) => ({
  ...c,
  eyebrow: c.status === "now" ? "Available now" : "Coming soon",
  ctaText: c.status === "now" ? c.cta || "Start this collection" : "Start with Human Foundations",
  ctaHref: c.status === "now" ? c.href || "/app" : "/app",
  head: c.courses.length ? `In this collection: ${c.courses.length} courses` : "",
  noteText: c.note || (c.status === "soon" ? "Coming soon. Start with Human Foundations in the meantime." : "")
}));
const first = VIEW[0];
---
<Layout title="Academy · The Practice" description="The curriculum school never offered. Practical lessons on demand to help you think, respond, communicate, decide, and lead in your real life." path="/academy" nav="learn">
<section class="view" id="academy">
  <div class="phero">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="eyebrow">InnerBoard Academy · Learn it</p>
        <a class="incl" href="/app#membership">Included with The Practice membership</a>
        <h1>The curriculum school never offered.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Practical lessons on demand to help you think, respond, communicate, decide, and lead in your real life.</p>
        <div class="ctas"><a class="btn btn-solid" href="#collections">Explore the Academy <span class="arr">→</span></a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ph photo hero-gfx"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="960" src="/images/practice/academy-books.webp" alt="Academy books on a shelf: Self Awareness, Confidence, Relationships, Communication, Decision Making, Leadership, Purpose, Parenting, Emotional Regulation"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band">
    <div class="wrap why">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why these skills matter</p>
        <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:0">You were taught math and history. Were you ever taught how to live your life, and how to lead it?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="points">
        <div><h4>Your reactions shape your relationships.</h4><p>Most regret starts with a response we never practiced. These skills give you more choice in hard moments.</p></div>
        <div><h4>Confidence comes from evidence.</h4><p>Learning a skill, then using it, builds trust in yourself in a way waiting never will.</p></div>
        <div><h4>Leadership starts inside.</h4><p>How you lead yourself shows up at home, at work, and with the people you love.</p></div>
        <div><h4>Experience alone isn’t enough.</h4><p>You can repeat the same year twenty times. Or you can spend twenty years getting better.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band paper" id="collections">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The {VIEW.length} collections</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Start with what you’re living right now.</h2>
      <div class="collections" id="collGrid">
        {VIEW.map((c, i) => <button type="button" class="coll" aria-pressed={i === 0 ? "true" : "false"}><div class="cimg"><picture><source srcset={c.dark} media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" /><img src={c.image} alt="" width="640" height="400" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></picture></div><span>{c.name}<small>{c.eyebrow}</small></span></button>)}
      </div>
      <div class="detail">
        <div class="stack" style="gap:14px">
          <picture><source id="collImgDark" srcset={first.dark} media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" /><img class="coll-hero" id="collImg" src={first.image} alt={first.name} width="640" height="400" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></picture>
          <p class="eyebrow" id="collEyebrow">{first.eyebrow}</p>
          <h3 id="collTitle">{first.name}</h3>
          <p class="lede" id="collDesc">{first.desc}</p>
          <a class="btn btn-solid" id="collCta" href={first.ctaHref} style="align-self:flex-start"><span id="collCtaText">{first.ctaText}</span> <span class="arr">→</span></a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="levelnote" id="collListHead" hidden={!first.head}>{first.head}</p>
          <ol class="lessons" id="lessons" hidden={!first.courses.length}>{first.courses.map((t, i) => <li><b>{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</b><span>{t}</span><small>Course</small></li>)}</ol>
          <p class="levelnote" id="collNote" hidden={!first.noteText}>{first.noteText}</p>
          <script type="application/json" id="collData" set:html={JSON.stringify({ c: VIEW })}></script>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">From lesson to daily practice</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Every lesson ends with a rep.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:14px">Lessons connect straight to the Practice Coach, so what you learn in the morning is something you try by the afternoon. Here’s a sample.</p>
      <div class="flow">
        <div><small>The lesson · 9 min</small><h4>The pause</h4><p>Why the space between what happens and how you respond is where most of your choices live.</p></div>
        <div><small>Today’s rep</small><h4>Pause once</h4><p class="quote">Before you answer the next text or comment that bothers you, wait. Take one breath and ask: what do I actually want here?</p></div>
        <div><small>Reflect in the app</small><h4>What happened?</h4><p>The Practice Coach asks what you noticed, what was different, and what you want to try next. Your streak grows.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band navy on-navy">
    <div class="wrap closer"><h2>Start where you are.<br>Build a life you’re proud of.</h2><a class="btn btn-solid" href="#collections">Explore the Academy <span class="arr">→</span></a></div>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
